        "V8 is based directly on V6, retaining rim_penetration_m = 0.025 m. It changes only the initial robot orientation from yaw 135 degrees to identity xyzw [0, 0, 0, 1] (yaw 0 degrees), preserving the original start XY and physical room route. Main-agent observations report successful T08 yaw-0 tray initialization, empty assisted-grasp ray candidates for T07 V6 yaw 135 and V5 yaw 180, and empty candidates after the V7 10 mm tray-height adjustment. Main static clearance estimates at yaw 0 place the right EEF at [4.9, -7.25, 0.8] m and tray center near [4.9, -7.04, 0.79] m; the estimated tray footprint x [4.747, 5.053] m and y [-7.259, -6.821] m clears the native hanging bookcase with minimum y -6.385 m and nearby sofa/coffee furniture. These are static estimates and an orientation-dependent initialization hypothesis, not confirmed native clearance, a confirmed failure cause or task success. Native confirmation remains pending. No physics, grasp algorithm, controller, ray settings, thresholds, props, supports, route, start XY, source runtime metadata or episode defaults change."
